{{!
    @template tool_vae/kept_text

    The text typed on the declaration page, given back when there is no form left: a sentence, then for each field typed
    its label and a field that can be read and copied. Nothing when nothing was typed. A textarea keeps its text as it is
    written: nothing stands between its tags and the text, and the label and the field touch.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\kept_text. The template holds no logic. Every
    value is escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * show - bool, whether anything was typed
    * intro - string, the sentence above the fields
    * fields - array of {id, label, rows, text}: the field, its label, its height and the text typed

    Example context (json):
    {
        "show": true,
        "intro": "Nothing has been recorded. Here is what you wrote, so that you can copy it.",
        "fields": [{"id": "tool_vae_kept_situation", "label": "Situation", "rows": 12, "text": "Help with getting up."}]
    }
}}
{{#show}}
<p>{{intro}}</p>
{{#fields}}<label class="font-weight-bold d-block" for="{{id}}">{{label}}</label>{{!
}}<textarea id="{{id}}" readonly="readonly" rows="{{rows}}" cols="70" class="form-control mb-3">{{text}}</textarea>{{/fields}}
{{/show}}
